{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model combining the high-performing scvi_n200 RNA encoder with the more capable imagenet_vit_l image encoder, using transformer aggregation and concat fusion. The validation accuracy of 0.7207 (F1: 0.6815) exceeds the previous multimodal baseline (0.6315 accuracy) and the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline (0.653 accuracy), suggesting potential benefits from the improved image encoder and aggregation strategy. However, the exact contribution of the image encoder versus the aggregation method remains uncertain due to limited direct comparisons isolating these factors."
}

